{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Wrap the build_transition parse in transition._parse_flags (or its caller) in a ParseError handler that renders via render_parse_error, matching the sibling handlers migrated in this changeset.","criteria":["regression","error-handling","correctness"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:163: `ns, _unknown = parser.parse_known_args(rest)` — no surrounding try/except","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:691-726: the only caller wraps `_parse_flags(flag_args)` in a try whose `except` clauses are `ConcurrencyMismatch` and `CommandError` only","`search_files` for `ParseError` in transition.py returns (no matches) — the module neither imports nor catches ParseError","Contrast: every sibling handler migrated in this changeset (compact.py:117, compact.py:545, _io/_cli.py:72, _io/_cli.py, claim.py:71, composer.py:339/654, session_log.py:300) catches ParseError and returns render_parse_error(exc)"],"finding":"transition._parse_flags calls build_transition(...).parse_known_args(rest) without catching ParseError; a trailing value-less flag (e.g. `rebar transition ID open closed --reason`) makes argparse raise ParseError, which escapes uncaught (the caller's try only catches ConcurrencyMismatch/CommandError) and there is no ParseError catch at the CLI dispatch boundary, producing an unhandled traceback instead of a clean diagnostic/exit code.","id":"0","impact":0.45,"location":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:163","norm_id":"n52c94c32100230e7","priority":0.45,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["`rebar transition <id> open closed --reason` (or `--class`/`--caused-by`/`--ref` as a trailing token with no value)"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In transition.py wrap the parse: `try: ns, _unknown = parser.parse_known_args(rest)` / `except ParseError as exc: raise SystemExit(render_parse_error(exc))` — or catch ParseError in transition_cli's existing try block and return render_parse_error(exc), matching claim.py/compact.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":true,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}}],"blocking":[],"change_fingerprint":"11c7a481721ba020","change_id":"I515cf762f40a37376d6ac5cf65e6475f2e12e155","coaching":[{"coaching":"Add a regression test covering uncaught ParseError from build_transition on value-less flag.","finding_refs":["0"],"move_id":"add-regression-test","move_name":"add a regression test","subject":"uncaught ParseError from build_transition on value-less flag"}],"coverage":{"llm_ran":true,"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"f